      ],
      "source": "https://crofton-nebraska.com/crofton-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The county’s original French name, L’eau‑qui‑court, meant “running water,” before it became Knox in 1873.",
